        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 66-year-old male, admitted on 10/06/2019 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, clinical examination revealed significant dyspnoea, reduced oxygen saturation, and audible expiratory wheeze. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation consistent with COPD, without signs of pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Blood tests demonstrated a mild inflammatory response. The patient was promptly commenced on controlled oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. He responded well to treatment with improvement in symptoms and oxygen saturation. He is discharged in stable condition with a course of oral steroids and optimised inhaler therapy. Please arrange follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
